  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile+avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best so far, while image-only resnet50 (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak. The critical open question is whether the weak image signal provides any complementary value when fused with the strong RNA signal. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests this by pairing the best-known RNA setup with the already-characterized resnet50 image encoder using the simplest fusion (concat). If it beats 0.591, multimodal fusion is a promising direction to exploit with better fusion or image encoders; if it does not, we can confidently deprioritize all resnet50 multimodal configs and focus remaining budget on RNA encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt). This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a fundamental design-axis question (is the image modality useful at all?) before committing further budget to downstream choices."
}

